{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.A3LiftFromDerivedOffBlock.geom_gives_lift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.A3LiftFromDerivedOffBlock.geom_gives_lift","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3OffBlockDerivation.lean#L281-L281","doc":"The derived (not fitted) off-blocks drive the even-face correction to the physical\n**lift** `κ_phys`, which strictly EXCEEDS `1` — an enhancement provably outside the\nself-adjoint branching route (`magnitudeFactor_le_one`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.A3LiftFromDerivedOffBlock.anti_self_adjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.A3LiftFromDerivedOffBlock.anti_self_adjoint","kind":"theorem","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3OffBlockDerivation.lean#L277-L277","doc":"The geometrically-derived off-blocks BREAK graded self-adjointness — they are the\nanti-self-adjoint (GGM/Stokes) amplitude the branching leaves free.  The bar\ninvolution `σ` is quantified as a genuine ring homomorphism applied to `B_geom`;\nthe self-adjoint reference value of `C_geom` is `−(σ B_geom)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.A3LiftFromDerivedOffBlock.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.A3LiftFromDerivedOffBlock.mk","kind":"ctor","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3OffBlockDerivation.lean#L271-L271","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.A3LiftFromDerivedOffBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.A3LiftFromDerivedOffBlock","kind":"class","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3OffBlockDerivation.lean#L250-L282","doc":"**§3b dependent conjecture — the A=3 lift closes via a DERIVED anti-self-adjoint\noff-block.**\n\n`@conjecture: dependent` (its content depends on the open geometric derivation of\nthe anti-self-adjoint off-block — `conj:qdifference-kernel-prolongation-symbol` /\nthe `qou-jqof` wall — supplying `B_geom, C_geom`).\n\nThe claim: geometrically-derived off-blocks `B_geom, C_geom` (INPUTS from the DM\nq-cubic, independent of the physical target) (i) **break** graded self-adjointness\n(`C_geom ≠ −(σ B_geom)`, the anti-self-adjoint amplitude the self-adjoint branching leaves\nfree) and (ii) drive the even-face correction to a physical **lift** `κ_phys > 1`\n(unreachable by the self-adjoint branching Schur complement, `magnitudeFactor_le_one`).\n\n**Why this is content-bearing and NOT a fit.**  In a *fit* `B` is solved from\n`κ_phys` (Route 2's `crossTerm_magnitude_surjective`).  Here `B_geom, C_geom` are\n*given* geometric inputs and the equation is a nontrivial *check* that the geometry\nlands the physics — false for generic off-blocks, and the strict inequality\n`1 < κ_phys` cannot even hold for the *self-adjoint* branching value (Part 3).\n**No instance is supplied**: deriving `B_geom, C_geom` IS the open keystone;\ndischarging this by *choosing* them to hit `κ_phys` would be the forbidden fit and\nis explicitly not done. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.branching_graded_selfadjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.branching_graded_selfadjoint","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3OffBlockDerivation.lean#L228-L238","doc":"**The branching super-matrix is graded self-adjoint** (`C = −σ B`).  The two\nbranching off-blocks are equal (`B = C`, symmetric real rotation) and bar-ODD\n(`σ B = −B`, from `offBlockNum_bar_odd`), so `−σ B = −(−B) = B = C`.  This is\nexactly the hypothesis of `BerezinianSelfAdjointCrossTerm.selfadjoint_crossTerm_bar_even`\n⇒ the cross-term is bar-EVEN.  Bar-even is the CORRECT parity for the ratio\n`r* = μ₃/c₃` (both moments bar-even), yet the magnitude is provably bounded `≤ 1`\n(Part 3): the branching supplies the right parity but the wrong *sign of\ncorrection*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.offBlockNum_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.offBlockNum_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3OffBlockDerivation.lean#L216-L226","doc":"**The branching off-block numerator `a − b` is bar-ODD** when the two 1-dim blocks\nare bar-conjugate (`b = σ a`).  The trivial/sign Markov weights ARE `q↔q⁻¹`\nconjugate (transpose-paired blocks with equal Borromean characters, Part 1), so\n`b = σ a` is the branching datum, threaded explicitly.  Result: `σ(a−b) = −(a−b)`,\nmatching the bar-ODD odd-face weight of `OddDecayWeightParity`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.observed_lift_unreachable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.observed_lift_unreachable","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3OffBlockDerivation.lean#L199-L211","doc":"**The observed A=3 lift `r* ≈ 1.585 > 1` is UNREACHABLE by the branching Schur\ncomplement (sorry-free).**  For any target `r > 1` — the observed `r* = μ₃/c₃`\nand the whole Route-5 acceptance band `[1.50, 1.71]` — the branching-derived\nmagnitude factor never equals `r`.  A genuine *enhancement* is structurally outside\nthe self-adjoint branching route; the lift must come from the anti-self-adjoint\n(GGM/Stokes) off-block the branching leaves free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.magnitudeFactor_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.magnitudeFactor_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3OffBlockDerivation.lean#L185-L197","doc":"**THE STRUCTURAL EXCLUSION (scope-(b), invariant cited: `sq_nonneg`).**  The\nbranching-derived even-face magnitude factor is `≤ 1` for ALL real diagonal blocks\n`a, b` with `a + b ≠ 0`: it is `1` minus a real square.  The self-adjoint\nHecke/Wedderburn branching Schur complement is a **REDUCTION**, never a lift —\nindependent of the sign of `a+b` (the square erases it).  This is the categorical\ncontent of \"every single-Markov-trace ingredient is bracketed *short*\": the\nbranching correction can only shrink, never enlarge, the naive value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.magnitudeFactor_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.magnitudeFactor_eq","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3OffBlockDerivation.lean#L172-L180","doc":"**The derived even-face factor is `1 − ((a−b)/(a+b))²` (sorry-free).**  Pure\nSchur-complement algebra: `t = (a−b)²/(a+b)`, `A = a+b`, so\n`(A − t)/A = 1 − ((a−b)/(a+b))²` (the physical `/2` normalization cancels).  This is\nthe *derivation's* output — the off-block is pinned, the factor is a fixed function\nof the two branching block values. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.magnitudeFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.magnitudeFactor","kind":"def","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3OffBlockDerivation.lean#L165-L170","doc":"The even-face magnitude factor `(A − t)/A` on the bar-even mass/C1 (`e₊`) face,\nwhere `A = D = oddDiag` is the even `(2,2)`-entry: the factor by which the full\nBerezinian face rescales the naive block-diagonal single-trace value.  The `/2`\nnormalization cancels in `(A − t)/A`, so this factor is normalization-independent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.crossTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.crossTerm","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3OffBlockDerivation.lean#L160-L163","doc":"The Berezinian cross-term `t = B·D⁻¹·C` assembled from the derived branching\noff-blocks (`B = C = offBlock`, `D = oddDiag`), in the `/2`-cancelled normalization. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.oddDiag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.oddDiag","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3OffBlockDerivation.lean#L155-L158","doc":"Odd diagonal super-block `D` (physical `D = (a+b)/2`; the `/2` cancels in the ratio,\nso `oddDiag a b = a + b`), coincident with the even `e₊` `(2,2)`-entry `A` under the\nsymmetric rotation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.offBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.offBlock","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3OffBlockDerivation.lean#L145-L153","doc":"Off-diagonal super-block numerator from the transpose-involution eigenbasis\nrotation of the self-adjoint mass endomorphism `diag(a, c, b)` on the `(3)↔(1,1,1)`\n2-cycle.  The physical off-block is `B = C = (a − b)/2`; the common `/2` (a fixed\northogonal-rotation normalization) **cancels** in the even-face magnitude ratio, so\nit is dropped here — `offBlock a b = a − b`.  (The self-conjugate `(2,1)` block is\ntranspose-fixed and decouples from the off-block.)  `a = m_{(3)}`, `b = m_{(1,1,1)}`\nare the branching block contributions — the derivation fixes `B`; it is NOT free\n(contrast Route 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.borromean_chars_equal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.borromean_chars_equal","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3OffBlockDerivation.lean#L134-L140","doc":"**The two transpose-paired 1-dim blocks carry the SAME Borromean character.**  So\n`m_{(3)}` and `m_{(1,1,1)}` differ only by their Markov weights: the off-block\n`B = (m_{(3)} − m_{(1,1,1)})/2` is `(w_{(3)} − w_{(1,1,1)})/2`, a pure *weight*\ndifference (bar-odd, Part 5). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.signChar_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.signChar_borromean","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3OffBlockDerivation.lean#L128-L132","doc":"Character of the sign (antisymmetric) 1-dim rep on the Borromean braid,\n`σᵢ ↦ −q⁻¹`: `((−q⁻¹)·(−q⁻¹)⁻¹)³ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.trivChar_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3OffBlockDerivation.trivChar_borromean","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3OffBlockDerivation.lean#L122-L126","doc":"Character of the trivial (symmetric) 1-dim rep on the Borromean braid\n`β = (σ₁σ₂⁻¹)³`, `σᵢ ↦ q`: `(q·q⁻¹)³ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}